We demonstrate that the ratio of decay widths for $ ar B^0 	o D^+ \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell$ and $ ar B^0 	o D_s^+ \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell$ diverges significantly from the expected heavy quark limit value of $1$. This deviation arises because the decay widths are governed by distinct hadronic form factors. We calculate these form factors using the light-front quark model, which incorporates the $SU(4)$ heavy-light quark symmetry. Our results indicate that the form factors for $ ar B^0 	o D^+ \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell$ and $ ar B^0 	o D_s^+ \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell$ differ substantially, leading to a marked discrepancy in the decay width ratios. Consequently, the experimental measurement of this ratio offers a valuable method for determining the $c$ and $s$ quark masses.
